  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Simplify the expression\n$$\\frac{(\\sqrt2-1)^{\\sqrt2}}{(\\sqrt2+1)^{-\\sqrt2}}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1$\n\nUse $(\\sqrt2-1)(\\sqrt2+1)=1$ and the negative-index law.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(\\sqrt2-1)(\\sqrt2+1)&=2-1\\\\(\\sqrt2-1)(\\sqrt2+1)&=1\\end{align*}$$\nHence the two positive bases are reciprocals.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{(\\sqrt2-1)^{\\sqrt2}}{(\\sqrt2+1)^{-\\sqrt2}}&=(\\sqrt2-1)^{\\sqrt2}(\\sqrt2+1)^{\\sqrt2}\\\\\\frac{(\\sqrt2-1)^{\\sqrt2}}{(\\sqrt2+1)^{-\\sqrt2}}&=\\bigl((\\sqrt2-1)(\\sqrt2+1)\\bigr)^{\\sqrt2}\\\\\\frac{(\\sqrt2-1)^{\\sqrt2}}{(\\sqrt2+1)^{-\\sqrt2}}&=1\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 54
  },
